WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.110
Good morning Hank, it's Monday.

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:02.789
I spent the weekend back home in Indianapolis.

00:00:02.789 --> 00:00:07.220
I actually got to ride a combine with Henry,
and learn about, like, contemporary American

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:09.910
farming practices from this amazing farmer
named Terry.

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:13.150
I know this is a very midwestern thing and
may not resonate with you, Hank, but A: I

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:18.060
love corn, B: I love gigantic machines, so
it was like, just a dream come true.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:19.760
Anyway, now I'm back on the Paper Towns set.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:21.760
We're shooting some of the abandonned minimall
scenes today.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:22.760
It looks incredible.

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:25.790
I can't show it to you, but I'm- agh, I'm
so excited.

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:26.970
Alright, I'll show you a little bit.

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:28.520
Remember this shirt from our childhood?

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:31.280
And speaking of our childhoods...

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:35.430
So Hank, on Thursday, you posted this picture
of us from circa 1981- by the way, significant

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:38.950
improvement in my pointing game now that we're,
like, a week into Pizzamas.

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:43.420
In response, Nerdfighters have been doing
some photoshopping, like us as a rap duo,

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:47.150
us playing cards... ah, Hank, the many gifts
of Pizzamas!

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:50.250
Nerdfighters, if you want to photoshop further,
there is a link in the dooblydoo.

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:53.930
Okay, I have to go back to the set.

00:00:53.930 --> 00:00:57.130
Justice: I am also here.

00:00:57.130 --> 00:00:58.130
(Laughter)

00:00:58.130 --> 00:00:59.130
John: Sorry.

00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:00.130
Hey, Nat, how's it going?

00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:01.130
Justice: Hey!

00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:02.130
Radar's also here.

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:03.130
John: Look at that camera.

00:01:03.130 --> 00:01:04.130
I have intense camera envy.

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:07.780
Okay, Hank, here's how 90% of my time on set
is spent: In between takes, I can, ah, listen

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:11.760
to Nat, and Justice, and Austin make jokes,
and they're always very funny, so that's nice.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:15.170
Then I watch the monitors, which I can't really
show you, except for, like, ah, this.

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:17.720
And then after every take there's all these
discusssions about, like, oh, should it be

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:19.990
bigger, should it be smaller, was the lighting...

00:01:19.990 --> 00:01:20.990
Nat: Aaaah.

00:01:20.990 --> 00:01:22.130
John: Uh oh... videobombed.

00:01:22.130 --> 00:01:25.869
And so everyone tries to figure out like how
to make the movie good, and then they're like,

00:01:25.869 --> 00:01:28.970
"Well, John, what do you think?", and I'm
like, "I think that this is amazing!".

00:01:28.970 --> 00:01:34.659
"Every take is ridiculously good, the camerawork
is much better than in my vlogging, the acting

00:01:34.659 --> 00:01:37.360
is a-astonishingly good!"

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:39.360
And then they all go back to talking about
lighting and stuff.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:40.890
So basically I don't really have a job.

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:42.140
But I have a chair.

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:47.080
Director Jake Schreier wears his suit every
single day to set, and his shoe game is alway

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:48.080
exceptionally strong.

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:49.080
How's the movie going?

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:51.880
Jake: The movie's going super well, John Green.

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:53.561
How do you feel?

00:01:53.561 --> 00:01:54.561
John: Good.

00:01:54.561 --> 00:01:55.561
The way you say my name is so weird.

00:01:55.561 --> 00:01:56.561
It's like one syllable.

00:01:56.561 --> 00:01:57.561
Jake Schreier: Johngreen.

00:01:57.561 --> 00:01:58.561
John: Yeah.

00:01:58.561 --> 00:02:00.720
The other big thing that happens on set is
I try to get advice from people, like-

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:01.979
Nat: Oh yeah.

00:02:01.979 --> 00:02:06.579
John: Like, uh, cinematographer David Lansenberg
taught me a little about using the camera.

00:02:06.579 --> 00:02:07.939
David: Let's frame from the bottom.

00:02:07.939 --> 00:02:08.939
John: Frame from bottom?

00:02:08.939 --> 00:02:09.939
David: Yeah, like this.

00:02:09.939 --> 00:02:12.260
John: Oh this is, this is when I look best?

00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:13.260
David: Like that.

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:14.260
(John laughs).

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:15.260
This is the best.

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:16.260
John: What do you think of this shot?

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:17.260
David: I like this shot.

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:18.260
John: Yeah.

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:19.260
David: A little bit more depth would be good.

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:20.260
John: How do I make more depth?

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:22.560
David: You know what, the, the background
over there is not bad.

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:23.560
Turn around.

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:24.560
John: Oh, this is nice.

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:25.560
Wait, where am I going?

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:26.560
David: There.

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:27.560
John: There?

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:28.560
David: There.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:29.560
You get the streets...

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:31.590
John: Then I go to the wardrobe department
and Mary Claire teaches me how to dress.

00:02:31.590 --> 00:02:32.629
All in all, it's pretty exciting.

00:02:32.629 --> 00:02:34.790
Oh, I just realized that I got a green screen
behind me.

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:36.380
You could do anything to my head!

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:38.450
I'm moving so you can't mess with my head.

00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:42.540
Hank, thank you for the lesson in stars and
planets; I will see you tomorrow.

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:43.540
P.S.

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:47.400
Nerdfighters, there are only four days left
in Pizzamas, so if you want my mustachioed

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:51.300
face on any of these items, you must order
in the next four days.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:52.379
Link in the dooblydoo, goodbye!

